// endpoint_register_workspaces.proto — RegisterWorkspaces: Emacs announces
// EVERY workspace it holds, in one call. HOST section.
//
// THE RE-ANNOUNCEMENT IS ONE CALL, NOT ONE PER WORKSPACE. When Emacs's link
// comes up on a daemon, or is promoted onto a successor, it re-announces every
// workspace it holds. Sent as one RegisterWorkspace per workspace, that is
// dozens of concurrent calls racing a daemon whose state database has ONE
// connection, and each registration also republished the roster, which re-reads
// the whole arrangement on that same connection: the calls queued behind each
// other's republications until they outlived Emacs's unary budget and the
// workspaces they were for were left with no daemon. Here the daemon registers
// the directories ONE AFTER ANOTHER, exactly as RegisterWorkspace registers
// each, and republishes the roster ONCE, after the last.
//
// EACH DIRECTORY HAS ITS OWN OUTCOME. One directory's refusal or fault never
// costs the others theirs: the answer carries one outcome per requested
// directory, in request order, and every one is settled before the answer is
// sent.
//
// IDEMPOTENT BY DIR, as RegisterWorkspace is: a directory already registered
// answers the ref it already has, and a directory named twice answers the same
// ref twice.

